/-!
# Six-dimensional gamma matrices and symplectic Majorana–Weyl spinors

Signature `(+,+,+,+,+,-)`, time last. `Cl(5,1) ≅ M₄(ℍ)`, so there is no real `8 × 8`
representation. Instead of complex `8 × 8` matrices this file uses the real `16 × 16`
representation, with integer entries, in which every identity is decided by the kernel.

* `Γ a`: the gamma matrices; `Γ7`: chirality, with `Γ7² = 1`;
* `qI`, `qJ`, `qK`: the quaternionic structure commuting with the Clifford algebra. The
  complex structure `qI` turns the 16 real components into 8 complex ones, and `qJ` is the
  antilinear map of the symplectic Majorana condition. With an extra `Sp(4)` index the
  (2,0) supercharges are the chiral spinors of this representation tensored over `ℍ`;
* `chargeC6 = Γ 5`: charge conjugation, with the symmetry table of `C q Γ^{(p)}`.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
namespace SYM6

/-- Real `16 × 16` integer matrices. -/
abbrev Mat16 := Matrix (Fin 16) (Fin 16) ℤ

/-- Diagonal of the metric, time last. -/
